    {
      "block_id": "525e5a7c9879::b0004",
      "section_id": "525e5a7c9879::s002",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "heading_path": [
        "Buyer's Guide Considerations for solicitations - Offer receipt",
        "Buyer's Guide"
      ],
      "markdown": "Offer receipt The method and location of bid receipt must be specified in the solicitation of offers. Here are the acceptable methods for offer submission and their conditions: In writing and submitted to the specified receiving unit: applicable for all ($) dollar values In writing and submitted directly to the buyer: for offers below $25,000 for goods and $40,000 for construction and services, including all applicable taxes Verbal submission by telephone: for offers below $25,000 for goods and $40,000 for construction and services, including all applicable taxes for any ($) dollar value in cases of documented extreme urgency, the director's approval is mandatory On electronic media (e.g., DVD s, USB keys, CD s) and submitted to the specified receiving unit By facsimile Canada Post Corporation\u2019s Connect service In situations where a particular method of response is deemed not acceptable, you must clearly indicate this in the solicitation document and in the Notice of Proposed Procurement (NPP).",
      "plain_text": "Offer receipt The method and location of bid receipt must be specified in the solicitation of offers. Here are the acceptable methods for offer submission and their conditions: In writing and submitted to the specified receiving unit: applicable for all ($) dollar values In writing and submitted directly to the buyer: for offers below $25,000 for goods and $40,000 for construction and services, including all applicable taxes Verbal submission by telephone: for offers below $25,000 for goods and $40,000 for construction and services, including all applicable taxes for any ($) dollar value in cases of documented extreme urgency, the director's approval is mandatory On electronic media (e.g., DVD s, USB keys, CD s) and submitted to the specified receiving unit By facsimile Canada Post Corporation\u2019s Connect service In situations where a particular method of response is deemed not acceptable, you must clearly indicate this in the solicitation document and in the Notice of Proposed Procurement (NPP)."
    },
